        "id": 1594,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both expressions are similar in that this refer to something being equivalent to something else. 並み in particular refers to measuring up to a certain standard, e.g. 彼の歌はプロ並みだ ('His singing is on par with a pro.'), while と同じくらい simply expresses an equivalence without implying a certain standard, e.g. 息子と同じぐらいの年 'around the same age as my son'.",
